<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms seek 30,000 tonnes of soymeal.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms seek 30,000 tonnes of soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean companies on Tuesday were seeking 30,000 tonnes of soymeal for arrival by May 30, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the buyers were aiming to purchase at around $280 a tonne c&amp;f, but may delay the plan due to high market prices hovering over $300 a tonne.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
